ion may limit NVIDIA's ability to enter other transactions that could help achieve other strategic objectives.\",\"If NVIDIA cannot complete acquisitions on time, including because of delays in regulatory approvals, NVIDIA may be unable to pursue other transactions.\",\"NVIDIA may not retain critical talent from an acquisition target.\",\"Technology may evolve and make an acquisition less attractive.\",\"Regulators could impose conditions that reduce the ultimate value of acquisitions.\",\"Investments in companies could create volatility and fluctuations in NVIDIA's results, including realized and unrealized gains or losses.\",\"NVIDIA could lose up to the full value of an investment.\",\"Many investee companies may not achieve profitability in the near term or at all.\",\"No guarantee of a return exists for investments in companies.\",\"Investments in private companies include investments in early-stage companies still defining strategic direction.\",\"Many securities held through private-company investments are non-marketable and illiquid at the time of initial investment.\",\"If investee companies are unsuccessful, NVIDIA could recognize an impairment or lose all or part of an investment.\",\"NVIDIA's investment portfolio contains industry-sector concentration risks.\",\"A decline in one or more industry sectors could increase impairment losses.\",\"Additional risks include diversion of capital and management attention.\",\"Additional risks include difficulty realizing a satisfactory return.\",\"Additional risks include difficulty obtaining governmental or regulatory approvals or financing.\",\"Additional risks include legal proceedings arising from a deal.\",\"Additional risks include possible failure of due diligence to identify significant issues.\",\"Acquisition-specific risks include difficulty integrating technology, systems, operations, and key personnel.\",\"Acquisition-specific risks include assumption of liabilities.\",\"Acquisition-specific risks include amortization expenses, goodwill impairment charges, and write-downs of acquired assets.\",\"Acquisition-specific risks include difficulty integrating accounting, forecasting, and controls.\",\"Acquisition-specific risks include an impact on NVIDIA's stock price.\",\"Acquisition-specific risks include fines, fees, or reputational harm if an acquisition cannot obtain regulatory approval or close.\",\"Acquisition-specific risks include increased debt and interest expense, as well as covenant-compliance requirements, when debt finances acquisitions.\",\"Acquisition-specific risks include dilutive equity issuances.\",\"Acquisition-specific risks include variability in performance-based consideration.\",\"Acquisition-specific risks include negative changes in economic conditions.\",\"Acquisition-specific risks include additional cybersecurity risks.\",\"Acquisition-specific risks include impairment of relationships with employees, vendors, and customers.\",\"NVIDIA says NVIDIA has experienced challenges integrating acquisition-target systems.\",\"Acquisition-target systems integration has been lengthy and costly for NVIDIA.\",\"Systems integration has caused delays in purchasing and shipping products.\",\"Systems integration challenges have impacted NVIDIA's results of operations and may continue to impact NVIDIA's results of operations.\",\"NVIDIA's filing says NVIDIA is finalizing an investment and partnership agreement with OpenAI.\",\"No assurance exists that NVIDIA will enter into an investment and partnership agreement with OpenAI.\",\"No assurance exists that a transaction with OpenAI will be completed.\",\"The MD&A says NVIDIA invested $17.5 billion in private companies and infrastructure funds during fiscal year 2026.\",\"NVIDIA's fiscal year 2026 investments in private companies and infrastructure funds primarily involved early-stage startups.\",\"NVIDIA's fiscal year 2026 investments included AI model makers that purchase NVIDIA products.\",\"Many of NVIDIA's fiscal year 2026 investments are illiquid and non-marketable.\",\"NVIDIA provided $3.5 billion in land, power, and shell guarantees to early-stage companies.\",\"If escrow and partners' operating activities are insufficient to cover a default, NVIDIA may assume the underlying leases or sublease the underlying leases.\",\"The filing says NVIDIA opened a research campus in Reykjavik, Iceland.\",\"The research campus in Reykjavik, Iceland, employs 4,200 people.\"]}", "type": "output_text", "logprobs": []}], "role": "assistant", "status": "completed", "type": "message", "phase": "final_answer"}], "parallel_tool_calls": true, "temperature": 1.0, "tool_choice": "auto", "tools": [], "top_p": 0.98, "background": false, "completed_at": 1792362487.0, "max_output_tokens": 10000, "max_tool_calls": null, "moderation": null, "previous_response_id": null, "prompt_cache_key": null, "prompt_cache_retention": "24h", "reasoning": {"context": "all_turns", "effort": "medium", "mode": "standard", "summary": null}, "safety_identifier": null, "service_tier": "default", "status": "completed", "text": {"format": {"name": "StatementGeneratorOutput", "schema": {"description": "Structured output for statement generation.", "properties": {"statements": {"description": "The generated statements from the answer", "items": {"type": "string"}, "title": "Statements", "type": "array"}}, "required": ["statements"], "title": "StatementGeneratorOutput", "type": "object", "additionalProperties": false}, "type": "json_schema", "description": null, "strict": true}, "verbosity": "medium"}, "top_logprobs": 0, "truncation": "disabled", "usage": {"input_tokens": 1067, "input_tokens_details": {"cache_write_tokens": 0, "cached_tokens": 1064}, "output_tokens": 1525, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 725}, "total_tokens": 2592}, "user": null, "access_programs": null, "billing": {"payer": "developer"}, "frequency_penalty": 0.0, "presence_penalty": 0.0, "store": false, "tool_usage": {"image_gen": {"inpu